# Normalize line endings to LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` gets CRLF working
# copies while the build generators (generate-sitemap, generate-llms) write LF.
# The result is that every `pnpm build` leaves client/public/sitemap.xml,
# llms.txt, and llms-full.txt showing as modified in `git status` with an empty
# `git diff` — pure line-ending noise that hides real changes to those files and
# invites an accidental CRLF-flip commit via `git add .`.
#
# LF is also load-bearing for patches/*.patch: pnpm applies those at install
# time and a CRLF conversion would break them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touch these.
*.mp4  binary
*.webp binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico  binary
